# Standard CODEOWNERS for repos under the github-repo-standard.
# Copy to the repo root as CODEOWNERS (or to .github/CODEOWNERS if
# the repo prefers it there; GitHub reads either location).
#
# Format: one line per pattern, pattern first, then the owners who
# must review changes under it. Owners are GitHub usernames or team
# names. Replace every placeholder below with the real owners for
# the repo before relying on this file: placeholder owners do not
# resolve, and an unresolved CODEOWNERS file enforces nothing.
#
# Keep the sensitive paths explicit: gate scripts, workflow files,
# and the rules page are the enforcement surface of the repo, so
# they carry named owners even when the default owner covers them.

# Default owner for everything not listed below.
* @PLACEHOLDER-OWNER

# Build law and gates: review required from the owning maintainer.
/docs/RULES.md @PLACEHOLDER-OWNER
/.github/workflows/ @PLACEHOLDER-OWNER
/tools/commit-gates/ @PLACEHOLDER-OWNER
